Dedupe the group-edit profile dropdown's fallback options and fix selection.

GroupUserProfileForm.vue's profileOptionsWithFallback getter builds
"fallback" dropdown options for any profile_uri used in the group's user
table but not present in the master profilesList (getAllProfiles()). Two
bugs combined to produce duplicate "Researcher profile" rows in the
group-edit dropdown:

1. It compared profile_uri values by exact string equality. The group
   search endpoint (GroupDAO.search(), which feeds this modal) returns
   profile_uri in expanded IRI form ("https://.../id/profile/x"), while
   getAllProfiles() returns the same profile in compact/prefixed form
   ("phis:id/profile/x"). Same profile, different string -- so every user
   row referencing it was treated as "unknown" and got its own fallback
   option, and (before this patch) never deduped against each other either.
   Confirmed on prod (2026-09-16): a group with 4 users all on the same
   valid profile produced 4 identical dropdown rows.

2. The select's bound :value used only normalizeUri() (trailing-slash
   trim), which doesn't resolve the same expanded-vs-prefixed mismatch, so
   even a correctly deduped option list wouldn't show as "selected" for
   rows using the other URI form.

Both are upstream bugs, present in 1.5.4, unfixed on develop 2026-09-16.

Fix: compare and dedupe profile_uri by canonicalUri() (the URI's path
local to its scheme+host or prefix) instead of exact string equality, and
resolve the select's bound value through the same canonicalization
(resolveSelectValue()) so the correct option is shown selected regardless
of which URI form the row's profile_uri happens to be in.

